NegRiskMarket has a two step verification process, in order to ensure reported outcomes are correct. First the UMA oracle has the possibility to flag the answer and after this there is a period of time in which the negRiskAdapterOperator can flag the result.
View following code for negRiskOperator: NegRiskOperator.sol View following code
The negRiskOperator can still change the answer in case he deems it to be incorrect, even after the UMA oracle has reported a valid outcome.
This leads to following problem: Currently the loan can be seized even if the negRiskAdapterOperator has flagged the result / the result is not yet determined.
In case the answer changes, it will lead to loss of collateral for the borrower.
Currently the _isQuestionPriceAvailable function checks if the UMA oracle OR the Market is determined. In case the UMA oracle returns a result, but this result is flagged and the market is not determined yet, the function will return true regardless.
```solidity
function _isQuestionPriceAvailable(
