The GigaNameNFT contract currently allows unlimited minting due to two key issues: confirmMint lacks a maxSupply check: This function does not validate the total number of minted tokens against a supply limit, allowing infinite token creation. mint function calls GameNFT._safeMint which assumes token IDs are sequential and represent the total supply, but this GigaNameNFT uses non-sequential IDs generated by hashing the username.
```solidity
function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes memory data) internal override {
uint256 _maxSupply = maxSupply();
if (_maxSupply != 0 && tokenId > _maxSupply) {
revert TokenIdExceedsMaxSupply();
}
```
GameNFT._safeMint does not consider burned tokens for calculating the total supply. While the maxSupply is currently set to 0 (infinite supply), this is a potential issue for future versions where a finite maxSupply might be introduced. If not addressed, these issues could lead to over-minting or incorrect enforcement of supply limits.

