In the mint function, the getSharesByStake will return 0, so mintShares will get called with amount == 0. Since, there hasn't been any deposits yet and totalShares == 0, it will go inside the if statement and try to amount -= DEADSHARES where DEADSHARES = 10 ** 3 constant. This will always revert with an underflow error.

