Assume a scenario where an NFT pool with assetRecipient set have the received funds sent directly to the assetRecipient. Now, suppose a user executes the swapTokenForSpecificNFTs(). The function _validateTokenInput() sends the required input funds, including fees to the assetRecipient. The function _payProtocolFee() tries to send the fees to the _factory. However, this function attempts to do so from the pair contract. The pair contract does not have any funds because they have been sent directly to the assetRecipient. So following this action the payProtocolFee() lowers the fees to 0 and sends this number to the _factory while fees end up at assetRecipient' instead of at the _factory. The fees then end up at assetRecipient instead of at the _factory.

