Stargate LP_STAKING_TIME contract clears and sends rewards to the caller every time the mint() or increaseLiquidity() functions are called. However, the assetState[asset].lastRewardGlobal variable is not reset to 0 even though the rewards have been transferred and accounted for on Stargate's side.

After a call to mint() or increaseLiquidity(), any subsequent call to mint(), increaseLiquidity(), burn(), decreaseLiquidity(), claimRewards(), or rewardOf() — which all internally call _getRewardBalances() — will either revert due to underflow or account for less rewards than it should, because assetState_.lastRewardGlobal has not been correctly reset to 0 but currentRewardGlobal (which is fetched from Stargate) has:

```solidity
uint256 currentRewardGlobal = _getCurrentReward(positionState_.asset);
uint256 deltaReward = currentRewardGlobal - assetState_.lastRewardGlobal;

function _getCurrentReward(address asset) internal view override returns (uint256 currentReward) {
    currentReward = LP_STAKING_TIME.pendingEmissionToken(assetToPid[asset], address(this));
}
```

Users will not be able to take any action on their positions until currentRewardGlobal is greater than or equal to assetState_.lastRewardGlobal. After that, they will be able to perform actions, but their position will account for fewer rewards than it should because a total amount of assetState_.lastRewardGlobal rewards is effectively nullified.

This will also DOS the whole lending/borrowing system if an Arcadia Stargate position is used as collateral because rewardOf(), which is called to estimate the collateral value, also reverts.

